    "topicLabel": "Sentence Correction & Usage",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "question": "John arrived at Mary's house a little before 9:00 P.M. but she was not there. She __________ (study, at the library).",
    "options": [
      "studied at the library",
      "has been studying at the library",
      "had studied at the library",
      "was studying at the library"
    ],
    "explanation": "Her studying was in progress at the moment John arrived, so the past continuous \"was studying at the library\" is right. \"Had studied\" would wrongly place the studying as finished before he arrived, and \"has been studying\" clashes with the past-tense narrative.",
