    "id": "mpsc-group-b-combined-(state-tax-officer-/-cooperative-audit-officer)-2024-english-q023",
    "subject": "english",
    "topic": "eng_sentence",
    "topicLabel": "Sentence Correction & Usage",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "question": "The Titanic __________ (cross) the Atlantic when it struck an iceberg.",
    "options": [
      "crosses",
      "had been crossing",
      "crossed",
      "was crossing"
    ],
    "explanation": "This is the classic past continuous plus past simple pattern: a longer action in progress (was crossing) is interrupted by a sudden one (struck). \"Had been crossing\" would need a second, later past reference point to be interrupted from, which the \"when\" clause does not supply.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
