    "topicLabel": "Modern Indian History",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "The first state to accept Subsidiary Alliance with the British East India Company was -",
    "options": [
      "Nizam of Hyderabad",
      "Raja of Tanjore",
      "Ruler of Mysore",
      "Nawab of Oudh/ Awadh"
    ],
    "explanation": "The Nizam of Hyderabad was the first Indian ruler to accept Lord Wellesley's Subsidiary Alliance in 1798.\n\n💡 Think of the Nizam as the first customer to sign up for a 'protection plan' -- he let British troops stay in his territory and paid for their upkeep, giving up independent foreign policy in return for security.\n\n⚠️ Mysore and Oudh accepted it later, so they're plausible but not first.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
