    "subject": "history",
    "topic": "gs1_history",
    "topicLabel": "Modern Indian History",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "In 1856, the British finally annexed Awadh under the -",
    "options": [
      "Subsidiary Alliance",
      "Dual System",
      "Doctrine of Lapse",
      "Permanent Settlement"
    ],
    "explanation": "Awadh was annexed in 1856 by Lord Dalhousie; the exam intends 'Doctrine of Lapse' as the answer, though strictly the stated pretext was misgovernance rather than a lapsed heir.\n\n💡 Picture a landlord who normally only evicts tenants with no heir, but this time evicts a tenant anyway by claiming 'bad housekeeping' -- Awadh's annexation bent the Doctrine of Lapse logic to grab a well-run, wealthy state.\n\n⚠️ Subsidiary Alliance is tempting because Awadh had earlier accepted it, but the actual 1856 annexation trigger given in most keys is the Doctrine of Lapse option.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
