    "options": [
      "Pitt's India Act of 1784",
      "Regulating Act of 1773",
      "Charter Act of 1793",
      "Charter Act of 1813"
    ],
    "explanation": "The Regulating Act of 1773 upgraded the Governor of Bengal to Governor-General of Bengal, with Warren Hastings becoming the first holder of that title.\n\n💡 It's like a store manager being promoted to regional head office boss -- 1773's Act promoted the Bengal Governor into the first Governor-General.\n\n⚠️ Pitt's India Act (1784) and later Charter Acts refined the system further, tempting people who know later reforms but not the original 1773 upgrade.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
