    "explanation": "The Simon Commission (1927) was boycotted because it had no Indian members, making it look like Indians were being denied a say in their own constitutional future.\n\n💡 Imagine a committee deciding your family's household budget with not a single family member in the room — that's why everyone walked out on Simon Commission.\n\n⚠️ Option about Muslim League support is a distractor mixing up Simon Commission with later communal politics.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
