    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Read the following points and choose the correct answer:\n1. The doctrine of judicial review is originated and developed in the USA.\n2. Judicial Review is the power of the judiciary to examine the constitutionality of legislative enactments and executive orders of both central and state governments.\n3. Judicial Review is needed to uphold the principle of the supremacy of the Constitution.\n4. Judicial Review power can also be exercise by both Union and State minister.\nWhich of the above statement is/are correct?",
    "options": [
      "1, 2 and 4",
      "Only 3",
      "1, 2 and 3",
      "1, 3 and 4"
    ],
    "explanation": "Judicial review originated in the USA (Marbury v. Madison), lets courts test the constitutionality of laws/orders, and protects the supremacy of the Constitution — all true. Statement 4 is false because judicial review is exercised by courts, not by ministers.\n\n💡 Judicial review is a referee's job on the field, not something the team captains (ministers) can do themselves — statement 4 hands the whistle to the wrong person.\n\n⚠️ Including statement 4 (mentioning both Union and State ministers) sounds official and government-related, tempting you to think it's part of the correct set.",
