    "explanation": "The Agricultural Produce (Grading and Marking) Act, popularly known as the AGMARK Act, was enacted in 1937 to certify the quality of agricultural produce.\n\n💡 AGMARK is like a quality-inspection stamp on food packets; the law that created this stamping system dates back to 1937.\n\n⚠️ 1936 and 1938 are close decoy years that test whether you actually remember the exact year versus just 'the 1930s'.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
