    "question": "Who first estimated the National Income in India?",
    "options": [
      "Dadabhai Naoroji",
      "RC Dutta",
      "VK RV Rao",
      "DR Gadgil"
    ],
    "explanation": "Dadabhai Naoroji made the first attempt to estimate India's national income (around 1867-68); V.K.R.V. Rao later made the first more 'scientific' estimate in 1931-32.\n\n💡 Naoroji is like the first person to roughly guess the total money in a piggy bank by hand; Rao came along later with a proper calculator and did it 'scientifically'.\n\n⚠️ V.K.R.V. Rao is commonly cited as the 'scientific' pioneer, which tempts many to pick him instead of Naoroji for the plain 'first' estimate.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
    "year": 2024,
    "paperId": "mpsc-group-b-combined-(state-tax-officer-/-cooperative-audit-officer)-2024-gs-ii",
