    "explanation": "Dampa Tiger Reserve in Mizoram covers an area of about 500 sq. km, making it one of the largest protected areas in the North-East.\n\n💡 Picture Dampa as roughly the size of a small district carved out purely for tigers and forest — about 500 sq km of protected wilderness.\n\n⚠️ 250 sq. km is a tempting round-number decoy for students who underestimate the reserve's actual size.",
