    "explanation": "The Iron and Steel industry is the largest mineral-based industry in India, forming the backbone of heavy manufacturing.\n\n💡 Iron and steel is the 'big machine' industry — almost every other factory (cars, ships, bridges) depends on steel, making it the giant among mineral-based industries.\n\n⚠️ Cement is also mineral-based and huge in volume, but in terms of overall industrial scale/importance, Iron and Steel is considered the largest.",
