    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "A child is swinging back and forth on a playground swing. At what point in the swing's motion is the speed of the child at its maximum?",
    "options": [
      "At the lowest point of the swing",
      "At the highest point of the swing",
      "Midway between the highest and lowest points",
      "Speed is constant throughout the swing"
    ],
    "explanation": "At the lowest point, all the swing's height (potential energy) has converted into speed (kinetic energy), so that's where it moves fastest.\n\n💡 Think of a skateboarder in a U-shaped ramp: they're slowest at the top edges and fastest zooming through the bottom — a swing is just a pendulum doing the same thing.\n\n⚠️ The highest point looks 'dramatic' so it's tempting, but that's actually where the child briefly stops to reverse direction.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
    "year": 2024,
