    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "What is the primary goal of Machine Learning (ML)?",
    "options": [
      "To replicate human intelligence exactly",
      "To automate tasks without human intervention",
      "To enable computers to learn from data and improve performance over time",
      "To create robots that can think and feel like humans"
    ],
    "explanation": "ML's core goal is letting computers find patterns in data and get better at a task over time, without being explicitly reprogrammed for every case.\n\n💡 It's like teaching a kid to recognize dogs by showing hundreds of dog photos, rather than writing a giant rulebook describing every possible dog.\n\n⚠️ Options about 'replicating human intelligence' or robots that 'think and feel' sound exciting but describe general AI/sci-fi, not what ML actually does.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
