    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "A specific learning technique that require several layers of neurons to increase learnable parameters with huge datasets is called -",
    "options": [
      "Machine learning",
      "Artificial Neural Network",
      "Deep learning",
      "Python"
    ],
    "explanation": "Deep learning uses many stacked layers of artificial neurons to handle very large datasets and learn complex patterns.\n\n💡 Think of it like a factory assembly line with many stations (layers) — each station refines the raw material a bit more before passing it on, letting the whole line handle a much more complex product.\n\n⚠️ 'Artificial Neural Network' is tempting since deep learning is built from ANNs, but the question specifically asks about the multi-layered, big-data technique, which is deep learning.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
