    "subject": "gk",
    "topic": "gs3_mizoram",
    "topicLabel": "Mizoram GK",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "A technique to generate high-resolution surface image of earth by expanding the radar aparture through motion of the mounting vehicle and the image quality not being affected by weather condition is -",
    "options": [
      "Light Detection and Ranging",
      "Synthetic Aperture Radar",
      "Optical Telescopic Vision",
      "Electron Macroscopy"
    ],
    "explanation": "Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) uses the motion of the satellite/aircraft to simulate a much larger antenna, giving sharp images that work even through clouds and at night.\n\n💡 It's like taking many quick photos while walking past a wall and stitching them into one super wide, super sharp panorama — except SAR does this with radar waves, so clouds don't block it.\n\n⚠️ Light Detection and Ranging (LiDAR) also does 'remote sensing' but uses light pulses, and it's affected differently by weather than radar-based SAR.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
    "year": 2024,
    "paperId": "mpsc-group-b-combined-(state-tax-officer-/-cooperative-audit-officer)-2024-gs-iii",
