    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "During the Pokhran – II nuclear test on 11th May 1998, how many nuclear bombs were successfully tested?",
    "options": [
      "3",
      "4",
      "5",
      "6"
    ],
    "explanation": "On 11 May 1998, India successfully tested 3 nuclear devices (a fission device, a low-yield device, and a thermonuclear device); 2 more sub-kiloton tests followed on 13 May.\n\n💡 Think of it as a two-part fireworks show: the big main show was on 11 May (3 devices), followed by a smaller encore two days later (2 more).\n\n⚠️ People often round the whole Pokhran-II episode to '5 tests', forgetting the question asks specifically about 11 May.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
