    "topicLabel": "Mizoram GK",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Crydoductylus vairengtensis is the new ______________ endemic to Mizoram discovered in Mizoram in November 2023.",
    "options": [
      "Fish species",
      "Orchid species",
      "Gecko species",
      "Earthworm"
    ],
    "explanation": "Cyrtodactylus vairengtensis is a bent-toed gecko described in November 2023 and named after Vairengte in Kolasib district, where it was collected; the genus Cyrtodactylus is the giveaway, since it is a large radiation of bent-toed geckos concentrated in Northeast India and Southeast Asia. Mizoram has yielded several new Cyrtodactylus species in recent years, making the state a hotspot for herpetological description. The place-name suffix -ensis in the species epithet is the standard clue that the animal is named after a locality.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
