    "options": [
      "Andra Pradesh",
      "Tamil Nadu",
      "Karnataka",
      "Kerala"
    ],
    "explanation": "Brucethoa isro, a parasitic deep-sea isopod found in the gill chamber of the Indian mackerel, was described by researchers working off the Kerala coast near Kollam and named to honour ISRO. Naming marine discoveries after Indian institutions has become a pattern in recent Kerala-based taxonomy, which is why the state is the answer rather than the space agency's home state of Karnataka. Karnataka is the trap precisely because ISRO's headquarters are in Bengaluru.",
