    "explanation": "The pair is built from two opposite runs of the alphabet: the first letters move forward A, B, C, so the next is D, while the second letters move backward Z, Y, X, so the next is W. That gives DW. Equivalently, each pair is a letter and its mirror image (A pairs with Z, B with Y, C with X, D with W), since the positions in every pair add up to 27.",
