    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "1, 2, 9, 28, ...?..., 126, 217",
    "options": [
      "65",
      "271",
      "56",
      "172"
    ],
    "explanation": "Every term is a perfect cube plus one: 0 cubed +1 = 1, 1 cubed +1 = 2, 2 cubed +1 = 9, 3 cubed +1 = 28, so the missing term is 4 cubed +1 = 65. The pattern is confirmed by the terms that follow: 5 cubed +1 = 126 and 6 cubed +1 = 217. Whenever a series jumps 1, 2, 9, 28 the gaps grow far too fast for an arithmetic or simple multiplicative rule, so test cubes first.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
    "year": 2024,
    "paperId": "mpsc-group-b-combined-(state-tax-officer-/-cooperative-audit-officer)-2024-gs-iii",
