    "topicLabel": "Reasoning & Aptitude",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "question": "44, 40, 34, ...?..., 16, 4",
    "options": [
      "26",
      "21",
      "28",
      "19"
    ],
    "explanation": "The differences themselves form an arithmetic sequence increasing by 2: minus 4, minus 6, minus 8, minus 10, minus 12. So 44 minus 4 = 40, 40 minus 6 = 34, 34 minus 8 = 26, and the chain checks out with 26 minus 10 = 16 and 16 minus 12 = 4. The missing term is therefore 26; the given tail values 16 and 4 are what let you confirm the rule rather than guess it.",
