    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "This is what I want.",
    "options": [
      "Preposition",
      "Adverb",
      "Pronoun",
      "Noun"
    ],
    "explanation": "In 'This is what I want', the word 'what' is a relative pronoun standing for 'the thing which'; it does duty twice, as the complement of 'is' and as the object of 'want'. It cannot be an adverb because it is not modifying the verb, and it cannot be a preposition because nothing follows it as an object. This nominal-relative use of 'what' is the one grammar point this question is testing.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
    "year": 2025,
    "paperId": "mpsc-inspector-of-excise-&-narcotics-2025-english",
