    "explanation": "A state party generally needs 6% valid votes in the state Assembly poll (with 2 seats), or wins at least 3% of Assembly seats, or wins 1 Lok Sabha seat per 25 (or part) allotted to the state; the vote-share figure in statement (ii) reads as 4% rather than the actual 6%, making (i)+(iii)+(iv) the better-fitting combination.\n\n💡 It's like a coupon rulebook where one clause has the wrong percentage printed on it — everything else checks out except that one number.\n\n⚠️ Statement (ii)'s '4%' sounds official and specific, which is exactly what makes a subtly wrong number convincing.",
