    "subject": "economics",
    "topic": "gs2_economy",
    "topicLabel": "Indian Economy",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Consider the following agricultural related revolutions in India: (i) Green revolution – Agriculture (HYV) production (ii) Yellow revolution – Oilseeds production (iii) Round revolution – Potato production (iv) Protein revolution – High agricultural production Which of the revolutions given above are correct?",
    "options": [
      "(i), (ii) and (iii) only",
      "(ii), (iii) and (iv) only",
      "(i), (iii) and (iv) only",
      "(i), (ii), (iii) and (iv)"
    ],
    "explanation": "All four pairings are the standard ones: Green Revolution for high-yielding-variety foodgrain production from the mid-1960s under M.S. Swaminathan and Norman Borlaug, Yellow for oilseeds under the Technology Mission on Oilseeds (1986), Round for potato, and Protein for the drive to raise agricultural and protein output announced in the 2014-15 budget as a second green revolution. Since none of the four is misstated, the 'all of the above' option is the answer, and every option that excludes one of them is wrong. Keep the rest of the colour list handy too: White for milk, Blue for fish, Pink for prawn or onion, Golden for horticulture and honey, Silver for eggs.",
