    "topicLabel": "Mizoram GK",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "The ‘5G High Level Forum’ appointed by the Government of India outlined the vision for 5G in the country. A key recommendation, distinguishing its vision from a purely commercial rollout, was to primarily leverage 5G for:",
    "options": [
      "Enhancing urban mobile broadband speeds to compete with global standards.",
      "Societal benefits by focusing on applications in healthcare, agriculture, and smart cities.",
      "Reducing the operational cost for telecom operators.",
      "Replacing all existing 4G infrastructures with indigenous 5G equipment."
    ],
    "explanation": "The Forum recommended using 5G's speed for real problems — telemedicine, precision agriculture, smart city services — so benefits reach beyond just urban mobile users.\n\n💡 It's like getting a supercar and using it as an ambulance and school bus too, not just for joyrides.\n\n⚠️ \"Enhancing urban mobile broadband speeds\" is the obvious commercial answer people expect from 5G, but the Forum's distinguishing call was societal/rural application.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
