    "question": "Water passes from soil to plant roots by a physical process called?",
    "options": [
      "Osmosis",
      "Diffusion",
      "Absorption",
      "Transpiration"
    ],
    "explanation": "Root hairs absorb water via osmosis, where water moves from the dilute soil solution into the more concentrated cell sap, across a semi-permeable membrane.\n\n💡 Water squeezes from a wet sponge into a drier sponge placed right next to it — the root cell is the thirstier sponge pulling water in.\n\n⚠️ \"Absorption\" is tempting as a general everyday word for the same process, but the specific mechanism tested is osmosis.",
