    "topicLabel": "Science & Technology",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "question": "Another name for ‘Dingdi puan tah’ is:",
    "options": [
      "Hrangkhupa se dar",
      "Sikeisen",
      "Khiangte zawng zim",
      "Vanpui saihrua"
    ],
    "explanation": "Dingdi puan tah and Hrangkhupa se dar are two traditional Mizo names for the same star, both appearing in the standard list of arsi names that the Mizos gave to the stars and constellations they used to mark seasons and jhum-cycle timing. Questions of this type simply pair alternative names within the traditional star nomenclature, so the reliable approach is to memorise the paired names rather than reason them out. The other options are unrelated terms drawn from folklore rather than alternate names for this star.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
