    "difficulty": "hard",
    "question": "A kind of engagement for marriage in Mizo tradition is:",
    "options": [
      "Lungvar",
      "Ran ngo zawng",
      "Khawnthiang",
      "Zawlpuan phah"
    ],
    "explanation": "Zawlpuan phah is the traditional form of betrothal in which the arrangement is sealed by the spreading of the zawlpuan, marking the couple as engaged before the full marriage negotiations and bride-price settlement are completed. It belongs with the other Mizo marriage-related terms an aspirant should keep together, such as palai (the go-between), man (bride price) and thutphah. The other three options are not marriage customs, which is what makes this a straight vocabulary recall.",
