    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Pointing to Mrs. D, Mr. R said, “She is the sister of my sister’s father”. How is Mrs. D related to Mr. R?",
    "options": [
      "Aunt",
      "Mother -in-law",
      "Grandmother",
      "Mother"
    ],
    "explanation": "Mr R's \"sister's father\" is simply his own father (they share a father), so \"the sister of my sister's father\" is the sister of Mr R's father — his paternal aunt.\n\n💡 Strip away the pronoun hops and it's just \"my father's sister\" — that's always your aunt.\n\n⚠️ \"Grandmother\" is tempting if you misread the chain as going up two generations, but it only goes up one generation.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
