    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Which of the following is not treated as part of the Indian Constitution?",
    "options": [
      "Preamble",
      "The Fundamental Rights",
      "Directive Principles of State Policy",
      "None of these"
    ],
    "explanation": "The Preamble (post Kesavananda Bharati case), Fundamental Rights and DPSP are all officially recognised parts of the Constitution, so none of the given options is excluded.\n\n💡 Like asking 'which of these three siblings isn't really family' when all three share the same parents — the honest answer is nobody.\n\n⚠️ Some assume the Preamble is 'just an introduction' and not real law, but courts have held it IS part of the Constitution, just not directly enforceable.",
