    "explanation": "In Indian census terminology, urban agglomerations with a population of one million or more are classified as Metropolises (or 'Million-Plus cities').\n\n💡 Crossing the one-million-resident mark is like a city 'levelling up' from a regular town to officially earning the 'Metropolis' badge in census records.\n\n⚠️ 'Megacities' sounds like the natural next step up in size, but that term is generally reserved for much larger populations (10 million+), not the one-million threshold this question asks about.",
